@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:security;architecture] personal-auth-never-adopts-operator-authority
Personal authorization MUST use only the fixed Pully-owned OAuth configuration and
the verified user's GitHub credential. Guest, missing, revoked, expired or failed
personal authorization MUST NOT fall back to environment/CLI GitHub credentials,
legacy account data or operator caches. This additive module MUST NOT activate a
public listener or expose legacy RPC. Source: Tavi's 21 Oct 2026 any-account GitHub
sign-in and anonymous public-browsing decision and its approved multiuser plan.

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:security] personal-vault-authenticates-its-stable-owner
GitHub access and refresh tokens MUST remain server-side and encrypted at rest with
authenticated encryption under an operator-supplied versioned key. The authenticated
context MUST include the stable account ID, immutable GitHub subject, credential
revision, provider and record format/key version. An unknown key, modified record or
record copied between accounts/revisions MUST fail without returning credentials.
No token, key or plaintext payload MAY appear in Debug output, status, logs or errors.
Source: Tavi's 21 Oct 2026 encrypted per-user credential-vault and identity plan.

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:security] personal-oauth-fixed-client-and-bounded-exchange
Authorization and token exchange MUST use the operator-configured Pully OAuth App,
fixed GitHub.com endpoints, a fixed HTTPS callback, random state and S256 PKCE.
Native input MUST NOT replace the app credentials, callback, provider or token URL.
Exchange MUST refuse redirects and bound its time, response and credential sizes;
provider error text MUST NOT escape. Every acquired access token MUST be verified
against GitHub's authenticated user before use. Source: Tavi's 21 Oct 2026 personal
GitHub authentication plan and GitHub's current OAuth App authorization docs.

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:security;product] personal-app-authority-is-not-inherited-scope
Public-read sign-in MUST retain public-read application authority even if GitHub
returns previously granted broader scopes. Private repository authority MUST require
an explicit upgrade and its actual repo grant. Expiring access/refresh responses
MUST retain both expirations and rotate the pair; reduced grants MUST NOT preserve
broader application authority. Scope MUST NOT bypass organization approval or SSO.
Source: Tavi's 21 Oct 2026 public-first and explicit private-access decision and the
current GitHub OAuth App scope and refresh documentation.

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:security;product] personal-repository-consent-is-source-and-session-bound
Repository consent MUST require a current personal session, fixed Pully-owned
GitHub repo authorization, the same immutable GitHub subject and a still-current
initiating session/revision at credential installation. Sign-out, source replacement
or a different selected GitHub user MUST deny the upgrade. Each Pully session MUST
authenticate its own maximum application authority; an older publicRead session
MUST NOT inherit a later session's private access. Missing authority in older durable
records MUST mean publicRead, and a reduced GitHub grant MUST still reduce effective
authority. Source: Tavi's 22 Oct 2026 own-account private-access requirement while
preserving the existing publicRead contract and canonical source isolation.

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:security;architecture] personal-session-is-bound-to-one-stable-user
Persisted personal sessions MUST contain only hashes of high-entropy Pully session
bearers. Session claims MUST authenticate their own hash, stable account, immutable
GitHub subject, generation, expiry and provisional confirmation deadline,
independently of credential envelopes. A
copied or expired session MUST NOT return a credential. Sign-out MUST revoke the
matching captured authority; unlink MUST revoke every captured authority and session
for that account. After an awaited identity verification, the current session and
credential revision MUST be rechecked before authority is published. Source: Tavi's
21 Oct 2026 per-user vault, revocation and cross-user isolation decision.

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:security] personal-legacy-link-requires-two-current-authorities
A legacy account link MUST require the actual authenticated legacy session and a
verified GitHub authorization. The legacy session MUST be rechecked when installing
the link. Email/login matching MUST NOT link identities, and an already-linked
immutable GitHub subject MUST NOT be reassigned or silently merge accounts. Linking
MUST NOT adopt legacy tokens, caches, account keys or unrelated data. Source: Tavi's
21 Oct 2026 compatibility and explicit linking decision.

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:security;architecture] personal-auth-native-proof-stays-in-bodies
The fixed personal-auth wire protocol MUST keep the native attempt proof and Pully
session out of browser URLs, callback URLs, logs and errors. A native client names
only its own random proof challenge; it MUST NOT supply provider/app configuration,
redirects, target accounts or application authority to public sign-in. A successful
single-use claim MAY return the newly issued Pully session once in its HTTPS body.
Unix timestamp fields MUST use seconds and pollAfterMs MUST use milliseconds.
Source: Tavi's 21 Oct 2026 server-owned authorization and bounded native handoff plan.

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:security;architecture] personal-attempt-is-single-use-and-proof-owned
An OAuth attempt MUST be bounded in count, start/poll rate and lifetime. Its state
MUST be random, stored only as a hash and consumed before code exchange. PKCE MUST
use a separate server-owned random verifier and S256 challenge. Status, claim and
cancel MUST require the initiating native proof using a constant-time verifier;
wrong proof MUST NOT consume another client's valid attempt. Claim MUST publish a
session at most once, and cancellation/expiry MUST deny late exchange or claim
results and revoke a session created during that race. Normal browser/background
handoff MUST NOT cancel an attempt. Source: Tavi's 21 Oct 2026 native OAuth plan.

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:architecture;security] personal-accepted-exchange-outlives-observer
Once callback state or a native claim has been accepted, dropping the HTTP observer
MUST NOT cancel the exchange/commit. Accepted work MUST remain tied to its original
attempt and verified subject. A newly issued session MUST remain provisional until
a bearer-authenticated session lookup confirms delivery before the original
attempt deadline. An unconfirmed session MUST expire at that deadline and MUST NOT
consume capacity needed by a later verified sign-in. Native clients MUST secure-store
the bearer before confirmation and MUST confirm before publishing the new source.
Confirmation MUST preserve one-use claim delivery and hash-only persistence; it
MUST NOT replay the OAuth code or return a prior bearer. Explicit cancellation MUST
retire publication authority; it MUST NOT make an already-consumed code reusable.
Source: Tavi's 21 Oct 2026 replay, source-guard and browser-return requirements,
clarified by the confirmed lost-claim recovery finding in the 22 Oct full auth review.

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:security;architecture] personal-refresh-rotates-without-resurrecting-sources
Refresh MUST serialize per stable account and revoke old captured authority before
using its refresh token. A rotated pair MUST be encrypted before retryable identity
verification; unverified pairs MUST NOT create authority. Every new access token
MUST verify the same immutable GitHub subject, and reduced scopes MUST reduce app
authority. Concurrent refresh MUST NOT reuse a consumed token, and sign-out/unlink
or a newer credential revision MUST deny stale publication or overwrite. A terminal
refresh rejection MUST revoke that account's sessions; transient transport or /user
failure MUST NOT invent a terminal rejection or discard a recoverable rotated pair.
Source: Tavi's 21 Oct 2026 refresh/revocation and current GitHub token rotation plan.

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:security;architecture] personal-http-surface-is-explicit-and-isolated
Personal auth MUST remain an explicit router factory with no production listener or
legacy RPC registration. Unconfigured discovery MUST report disabled without loading
operator account/provider state. Configured handlers MUST accept only their fixed
typed paths, reject legacy session/Access credentials, bound bodies/query data and
return fixed credential-safe failures with no-store responses. Only a Pully personal
bearer may authenticate personal session methods. Browser callback cookies MUST NOT
choose identity or authorize a claim; callback content MUST contain no credentials,
code or state and MUST forbid referrer disclosure. Source: Tavi's 21 Oct 2026 public
auth boundary and later external registration/deployment prerequisite decision.

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:security;architecture] personal-host-startup-does-not-guess-authority
The typed auth-host factory MUST accept only explicit isolated storage, validated
Pully OAuth configuration and in-memory vault keys from trusted startup. Missing
configuration MUST create only disabled discovery without opening storage; invalid
configured startup MUST fail with a fixed path- and credential-safe error. It MUST
NOT load environment/HOME defaults, seed legacy accounts or bind a listener. The
separate listener owner MUST control the storage path and its ancestors during
startup. Source: Tavi's 22 Oct 2026 requirement to complete concrete configured-host
composition while preserving the 21 Oct personal/legacy authority boundary.
